The Republic is helpless against this
sinister threat, and the brave and wise
JEDI KNIGHTS remain fearful of Ro's
fabled NAMELESS creatures, which the
Jedi have learned are very real, and
very deadly&hellip;.}}

==Plot summary==
In the [[Arkorayal Cabaret Cantina]] in [[Bri-Phrang City]], [[Eriadu]], the [[Mikkian]] [[Zeen Mrala-Talisola|Zeen Mrala]] [[Musician|sings]] a [[Unidentified Corellian funeral shanty|funeral shanty]] to the assembled audience, as she has nightly for a long while. In the crowd are the [[hologram]]s of [[Jedi]] who [[Death|died]] in the [[Nihil conflict]]. As her singing builds in intensity, three new holograms take shape: those of [[Farzala Tarabal]], [[Torban Buck]], and [[Lula Mrala-Talisola|Lula Talisola]]. All three had gone missing during the [[Destruction of Starlight Beacon|destruction of Starlight Beacon]] a [[Standard year|year]] earlier, but never confirmed dead. Their surprise appearance rattles Mrala, and she darts off the stage and into the outside air.

Mrala is followed by her [[droid]] friend [[5A-G3]]. Mrala demands to know who had those holograms projected, and she figures it was the [[Tarsunt]] [[Jackaby Snell]]. She confronts the man, who explains that per [[Galactic Republic|Republic]] custom, individuals missing and presumed dead for a time of one year are officially declared dead. As the anniversary of [[Starlight Beacon]]'s destruction was one year and one [[Standard day|day]] ago, he decided to honor them. Their conversation is interrupted by [[Jedi Knight]] [[Qort]], who informs Mrala of [[Marchion Ro]]'s [[Pra-Tre Veter's execution|murder]] of [[Jedi]] [[Grand Master]] [[Pra-Tre Veter]] and invites her to talk outside.

On the roof of the [[cantina]], Mrala and Qort embrace as they experience their grief for their friends. Hoping to cheer Mrala up, 5A-G3 invites her to examine the list of open cases of potential leads for the whereabouts of Lula Talisola and the others. To broaden her search, Mrala has the droid display all of the cases they have discarded throughout their search. Her thoroughness pays off, as she finds a case reading "I have what the Mikkian wants." The lead stems from a [[warlord]] on the [[moon]] [[Bracront]] and dates back several [[Standard week|weeks]]; Mrala missed the message because the [[Padawan]]s she had monitoring chatter while she was away on a mission felt the lead did not hold promise. Upon closer examination, they find that on Bracront, a sole Nihil warlord by the name of Tartak Vil established a small fiefdom bolstered by the cooperation of locals. Knowing that with the [[Guardian Protocols]] in place the [[Jedi Council]] would not permit the mission, the pair decide to go rogue and pursue the mission anyway.

Zeen Mrala reflects on how a year prior, on [[Corellia]] while Talisola was dealing with Starlight Beacon's imminent demise, she recorded a [[holomessage]] professing her love for Talisola. She wonders if the other girl ever received the message.

On Bracront, a sizable group of Mikkians has assembled around [[Tartak Vil's fortress]], all hoping the warlord has what they want. Soon, Zeen Mrala arrives and finds that the others have been waiting for weeks to get an audience with the warlord and want her help to storm the fortress. Qort reluctantly agrees to help. The Mikkians charge, but they are stopped by Vil's [[Pau'an]] guards. The two factions engage in a skirmish, and in the chaos Mrala bursts into the fortress, taking out the guards inside.

Zeen Mrala bursts into Vil's chambers, to the warlord's surprise. She pins Vil to the wall with a [[spear]] and demands to see Lula. The warlord, however, softens. Vil says the only thing that got them through was a holomessage, the very holomessage Mrala had sent to Talisola a year prior. Mrala realizes that Tartak Vil is the disguise of Lula Talisola. She takes off her helmet, and the two kiss.

==Development==
Older teased two panels from the issue in a [[November]] 2023 newsletter. In the newsletter, he also shared his joy that the ''Adventures'' cast of characters, his "chaos children," would be back.<ref name="Newsletter">{{Twitter|SWSplashPagePod|status/1729535030177718319|''Star Wars'' Splash Page|quote=Writer @djolder, in his newsletter (subscribe at https://danieljosolder.substack.com), has a two-panel preview From Dec. 13's #StarWars #TheHighRepublicAdventures Phase III #1, w/art by Harvey Tolibao, colors by Michael Atiyeh & letters by Comicraft. #StarWarsComics #TheHighRepublic|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/U9ldV}}</ref>

